<title>USA: Battle Mountain Gold confirms end of Niugini talks.</title>
<headline>Battle Mountain Gold confirms end of Niugini talks.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Battle Mountain Gold Co said on Friday that discussions have ended with its 50.5 percent owned subsidiary, Niugini Mining Ltd, because of valuation issues.</p>
<p>The company said the talks concerned the purchase of the remaining shares of Niugini that Battle Mountain Gold does not currently own.</p>
<p>The Sydney, Australia-based Niugini said in an earlier statement that the A$4.00 per share merger price offered by Battle Mountain was insufficient.</p>
</text>
